<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 18.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - June 18.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for June 18</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	     AH	   PH 13 PCT    PH 14  PCT</p>
<p>    Jun    184.00 -0.5  192.50 -0.5  196.00 n/c   206.50 n/c</p>
<p>    Jul    181.00 -0.5  189.50 -0.5  193.00 n/c   205.50 n/c</p>
<p>    Aug    176.50 -0.5  186.00 -0.5  189.50 n/c   203.50 n/c</p>
<p>    Sept   176.50 -0.5  186.00 -0.5  189.50 n/c   203.50 n/c</p>
<p>    Oct    178.50 -0.5  187.00 -0.5  190.50 n/c   204.50 n/c</p>
<p>    Nov    179.50 -0.5  188.00 -0.5  191.50 n/c   205.50 n/c</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat decreased by A$0.50 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>    National FOB	174.50</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  150.00	    Port Adelaide	 151.50</p>
<p>    Gladstone     150.25	    Port Giles	    152.25</p>
<p>    Brisbane	148.00	    Wallaroo		150.00</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    147.00</p>
<p>    Newcastle     150.00	    Port Lincoln	  153.25</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   150.50	    Thevenard	     148.25</p>
<p> Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 149.50	     Esperance	    154.75</p>
<p>    Portland	150.50	     Albany		 155.75</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    157.75</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    155.75</p>
<p>AWB MARKET COMMENTARY: World wheat prices were slightly lower overnight in quiet trade.</p>
<p>AWB cash bids for New South Wales A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>			 1996/97 crop		1997/98 crop</p>
<p>    ASW/APW	  A$174.00 Newcastle	A$164.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    AH1:	     A$184.00 Newcastle	A$177.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    PH 13:	   A$209.00 Newcastle	A$192.00 Newcastle</p>
<p>    Feed Barley    A$147.50 *State avge    A$125.00 *State avge</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	ex farm Nov/Dec</p>
<p>    Sorghum	  A$156.00 Newcastle	No bid</p>
<p>    Triticale	A$159.00 *State avge     A$119.00 *ex farm</p>
<p>			 ex farm June/July	 Dec/Jan</p>
<p>NOTES: The multigrade indicator price represents the AWB's view of the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered by the AWB.</p>
<p>ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; PW = Premium White; Percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>* Prices vary between regions.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
